d the closest match  in our available inventory so that'll be  something to be very exciting i think  for most  once that is available so those are i  would say the best options  for that purpose  thank you chris we have one last  question here and it's for britney  can you share the guidelines on media  selection for different cell types  so there's a lot of different media  options out there  as i mentioned even just basal media  there's a  more than 100 kind different kinds and  there's a breadth of many supplements  you can choose from as well  it's really cell type dependent you know  the first place i start  when the culture can do cell type is the  scientific literature  looking at protocols found there  of course your colleagues at your  university for instance may um will also  be a great resource there  the other thing i might recommend  especially for for newer products that  are out there and for  specialty cell types would just be going  to the thermofisher.com website and  typing in your  cell type and see if we have any cell  type specific options there for you  we have a wide variety of stem cell  media for instance  some of them are new for instance so  they might not be in the literature  quite yet but that doesn't mean that  they um  wouldn't be a great tool for culturing  your cells so  just doing a quick search there um i  would recommend  as well we have lots of great products  there  well thank you brittany this wraps up  our gibco galaxy tour webinar today  we would like to thank brittany balhaus  and chris scanlon  for sharing their knowledge and cell  culture experience  and we would also like to thank the  audience for joining us today  and for their interesting questions for  questions we are unable to answer today  we will follow up with an answer via  email we hope all of you have gained  knowledge today that will enhance your  lab skills in the future  we would also like to thank lab roots  for underwriting today's educational  webcast